      "help_en": "The idempotency token generated by the caller as a globally unique value (UUID recommended), with a maximum length of 64 characters. Within approximately 24 hours after the first successful request, a duplicate request that carries the same ClientToken and identical request parameters directly returns the consumerId from the first creation without creating a new consumer. A request that carries the same ClientToken but different request parameters returns IdempotentParameterMismatch. If the first request is still being processed, IdempotentProcessing is returned. If this parameter is not specified, idempotency control is disabled and the behavior is consistent with earlier versions",
